\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Are there fixed constants $\varepsilon ,\delta >0$ and a deterministic polynomial-time reduction taking every binary End-of-Line instance of length N to an $\varepsilon$-approximate generalized circuit of full encoding length O(N(log $N)^b)$, for one fixed b, such that every assignment satisfying all but a $\delta $ fraction of its gates has polynomial encoding and can be decoded in polynomial time to an End-of-Line solution?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Are there fixed constants $\varepsilon ,\delta >0$ and a deterministic polynomial-time reduction taking every binary End-of-Line instance of length N to an $\varepsilon$-approximate generalized circuit of full encoding length O(N(log $N)^b)$, for one fixed b, such that every assignment satisfying all but a $\delta $ fraction of its gates has polynomial encoding and can be decoded in polynomial time to an End-of-Line solution?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-PCP-for-PPAD-conjecture-a-quasilinear-reduction-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

